<speak>No, there is nothing I need to attend to at the moment. We have family plans later, but I left room for this call. I am trying to be more realistic about that. Previously I would promise to be ready, then begin a business conversation just as everyone was preparing to leave. It was unfair to them and not particularly helpful to the person on the telephone either. I am learning to make room for a conversation rather than squeeze it into a gap and hope it behaves like a short message.</speak>